<p>Notes:</p>
<ol>
<li>All the approaches shown in the benchmark rely on the fact that allowed chars are static or rarely change so you can build collection single time and reuse it</li>
<li><code>SearchValues</code> relies on utilizing SIMD instructions for <code>IndexOfAny</code> and similar operations so it will give performance only if a) those are present (should be the case for quire a lot of modern CPUs especially x86 architecture) b) the input is relatively long, in my other bench with single character string <code>IndexOfAny</code> have shown worse timing compared to the iteration approach with <code>FrozenSet</code>/<code>SearchValues</code></li>
</ol>

Q: Missing response_type parameter in Agent Engine OAuth2 Authorization request A: <p>There is currently no official configuration option in Agent Engine to manually force this parameter, but you can proxy the authorization request through a middleware that injects the missing parameter before forwarding to your IdP.</p>
<pre><code>from flask import Flask, request, redirect

app = Flask(__name__)

AUTH_URI = &quot;https://your-idp.com/oauth2/v1/authorize&quot;

@app.route(&quot;/oauth2-proxy/authorize&quot;)
def authorize():
    params = request.args.to_dict()
    params.setdefault(&quot;response_type&quot;, &quot;code&quot;)
    query_string = &quot;&amp;&quot;.join(f&quot;{k}={v}&quot; for k, v in params.items())
    return redirect(f&quot;{AUTH_URI}?{query_string}&quot;)

if __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:
    app.run(port=8080)
</code></pre>
<p>You can then point your agent engine's `authorization_uri` to this proxy instead of directly to your IdP, and report the bug via the [Google Cloud issue tracker](<a href="https://issuetracker.google.com" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://issuetracker.google.com</a>) referencing the missing `response_type` parameter so it gets patched in the Agent Engine request generator.</p>

Q: Shiny app - A conditional selectInput with renderUI persists despite condition no longer being met A: <p>A better solution was suggested by lailaps, in a comment to the original question.</p>
<p>His solution (without using freezeReactiveValue):</p>
<pre class="lang-r prettyprint-override"><code># Packages and data: ----
library(shiny)
library(bslib)

samlet_liste &lt;-
  list(
    &quot;termin1&quot; = list(&quot;variant1&quot; = list(&quot;model1&quot; = &quot;1&quot;, &quot;model2&quot; = &quot;2&quot;, &quot;model3&quot; = &quot;3&quot;),
                     &quot;variant2&quot; = list(&quot;model1&quot; = &quot;1&quot;, &quot;model2&quot; = &quot;2&quot;, &quot;model3&quot; = &quot;3&quot;)),
    &quot;termin2&quot; = list(&quot;variant1&quot; = list(&quot;model1&quot; = &quot;1&quot;, &quot;model2&quot; = &quot;2&quot;, &quot;model3&quot; = &quot;3&quot;),
                     &quot;variant2&quot; = list(&quot;model1&quot; = &quot;1&quot;, &quot;model2&quot; = &quot;2&quot;, &quot;model3&quot; = &quot;3&quot;))
  )

# UI: ----
ui &lt;- fluidPage(

  theme = bs_theme(version = 5, bootswatch = &quot;cerulean&quot;),

  sidebarLayout(
    sidebarPanel(
      width = 3,
      selectInput(&quot;termin&quot;, &quot;Termin:&quot;, names(samlet_liste)),
      selectInput(&quot;variant&quot;, &quot;Variant:&quot;, choices = NULL),
      selectInput(&quot;model&quot;, &quot;Model:&quot;, choices = NULL),
      uiOutput(&quot;conditional_input&quot;)
    ),

    mainPanel(

    )
  )
)


# Server: ----
server &lt;- function(input, output, session){

  # Resets variant and model when termin is changed:
  observeEvent(input$termin, {
    req(input$termin)

    updateSelectInput(
      session,
      &quot;variant&quot;,
      choices = c(&quot; &quot;, names(samlet_liste[[input$termin]])),
      selected = &quot; &quot;
    )

    updateSelectInput(
      session,
      &quot;model&quot;,
      choices = c(&quot; &quot;),
      selected = &quot; &quot;
    )
  })

  # Resets model when variant is changed:
  observeEvent(input$variant, {
    req(input$variant)

    updateSelectInput(
      session,
      &quot;model&quot;,
      choices = c(&quot; &quot;, names(samlet_liste[[input$termin]][[input$variant]])),
      selected = &quot; &quot;
    )
  }
  )

  # Makes conditional selectInput:
  output$conditional_input &lt;- renderUI({
    req(input$variant)

    if (input$variant == c(&quot;variant1&quot;)) {
      selectInput(&quot;cond&quot;, &quot;Conditional:&quot;, choices = c(&quot;none&quot;, &quot;cond1&quot;, &quot;cond2&quot;))
    } else {
      NULL
    }
  })

}

shinyApp(ui = ui, server = server)
</code></pre>
